f(x)=\frac{5\mathopen{}\left(x^{2}+4\right)\cot\mathopen{}\left(x\right)}{1-\cos\mathopen{}\left(x\right)\csc\mathopen{}\left(x\right)}=\frac{5\mathopen{}\left(x^{2}+4\right)\cot\mathopen{}\left(x\right)}{1-\cot\mathopen{}\left(x\right)}
Using the quotient rule to differentiate we get,
f'(x)=\frac{d}{dx}(\frac{5\mathopen{}\left(x^{2}+4\right)\cot\mathopen{}\left(x\right)}{1-\cos\mathopen{}\left(x\right)\csc\mathopen{}\left(x\right)})=5\frac{\frac{d}{dx}[\left(x^{2}+4\right)\cot\mathopen{}\left(x\right)]\cdot (1-\cot\mathopen{}\left(x\right))-\frac{d}{dx}[1-\cot\mathopen{}\left(x\right)]\cdot \left(x^{2}+4\right)\cot\mathopen{}\left(x\right)}{(1-\cot\mathopen{}\left(x\right))^2}
=5\frac{[2x\cdot \cot\mathopen{}\left(x\right) - \csc^{2}\mathopen{}\left(x\right) \cdot (x^{2}+4)]\cdot  (1-\cot\mathopen{}\left(x\right))-[\csc^{2}\mathopen{}\left(x\right)]\cdot \left(x^{2}+4\right)\cot\mathopen{}\left(x\right)}{(1-\cot\mathopen{}\left(x\right))^2}
=\frac{5\mathopen{}\left(2x\cot\mathopen{}\left(x\right)-\left(x^{2}+4\right)\csc^{2}\mathopen{}\left(x\right)-2x\cot^{2}\mathopen{}\left(x\right)\right)}{\left(1-\cot\mathopen{}\left(x\right)\right)^{2}}
